+# CLAUDE.md
+
+This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.
+
+## Repository Overview
+
+ROCm Systems is a super-repo (monorepo) consolidating ~28 ROCm systems projects that were previously separate GitHub repositories. Each project under `projects/` builds independently and is released as a distinct package. The `shared/` directory contains cross-project dependencies that don't produce their own packages.
+
+## Repository Structure
+
+```
+projects/          # Individual ROCm projects (each was formerly its own repo)
+  amdsmi/          # AMD System Management Interface library
+  aqlprofile/      # AQL profiler
+  clr/             # Compute Language Runtime (OpenCL + HIP runtime)
+  hip/             # HIP runtime
+  hipfile/         # HIP file I/O library
+  hip-tests/       # HIP test suite
+  rccl/            # ROCm Collective Communications Library
+  rdc/             # ROCm Data Center tool
+  rocdecode/       # Video decode library
+  rocjpeg/         # JPEG decode library
+  rocprofiler/     # ROCm profiler (legacy)
+  rocprofiler-compute/   # ROCm compute profiler (Python-based, uses Ruff)
+  rocprofiler-register/  # Profiler registration library
+  rocprofiler-sdk/       # Profiler SDK (C/C++)
+  rocprofiler-systems/   # CPU/GPU application tracing with binary instrumentation
+  rocr-runtime/          # ROCr runtime (HSA)
+  roctracer/             # ROCm tracer
+  ...
+shared/            # Cross-project shared code
+  ctest/           # Shared CTest integration (YAML-based test categorization)
+  kpack/           # Kernel packing utilities
+emulation/         # Emulation projects (rocjitsu)
+experimental/      # Experimental projects (perf-dkms, perfxpert)
+test/therock/      # TheRock integration tests
+python/            # Python utilities (rocm-bootstrap)
+```
+
+## Build System
+
+Each project has its own CMakeLists.txt and builds independently. There is **no top-level CMakeLists.txt**. Build a project by entering its directory:
+
+```bash
+cd projects/<project-name>
+cmake -B build -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=amdclang++ .
+cmake --build build --parallel
+```
+
+Some projects may require additional CMake flags (e.g., `-DROCM_PATH=/opt/rocm`). Check each project's CMakeLists.txt for available options.
+
+### Version
+
+Project versions are typically defined in a `VERSION` file in the project root (e.g., `projects/rocprofiler-sdk/VERSION`) and extracted by CMake.
+
+## Testing
+
+Tests use **CTest** and/or **Google Test**. Build with tests enabled, then run:
+
+```bash
+# Run all tests
+ctest --test-dir build
+
+# Run with verbose output
+ctest --test-dir build -V
+
+# Run tests matching a label or name
+ctest --test-dir build -R <test_name_pattern>
+ctest --test-dir build -L <label>
+```
+
+### Test Categories (shared/ctest)
+
+Projects using the shared test category system define `test_categories.yaml` with tiered labels: `quick` → `standard` → `comprehensive` → `full`. Tests in lower tiers inherit labels from higher tiers, so `ctest -L standard` includes all `quick` tests too.
+
+```bash
+ctest --test-dir build -L quick          # Fast sanity checks
+ctest --test-dir build -L standard       # PR-level tests
+ctest --test-dir build -LE quick_exclude # Exclude specific tests
+```
+
+## Formatting and Linting
+
+### Pre-commit (recommended)
+
+```bash
+pip install pre-commit
+pre-commit install
+```
+
+The root `.pre-commit-config.yaml` enforces:
+- **clang-format** (v18.1.4 mirror) for C/C++ — uses `-style=file`, so each project's `.clang-format` is respected
+- **black** (v22.10.0) for Python
+- **gersemi** for CMake formatting
+- **trailing-whitespace**, **end-of-file-fixer**, **check-yaml**, **check-added-large-files**
+
+Some projects have their own `.pre-commit-config.yaml` (amdsmi, rdc, rocm-smi-lib, rocprofiler-systems) and are excluded from the root config.
+
+### C++ Formatting
+
+Each project has its own `.clang-format`. Common settings: 4-space indent, left-aligned pointers, brace wrapping after control statements, column limit 90-100.
+
+### Python Formatting
+
+- Most projects use **black**
+- **rocprofiler-compute** uses **Ruff** (see `.ai/rules/` in that project)
+
+### CMake Formatting
+
+- **gersemi** is the standard CMake formatter (replaces cmake-format)
+
+## Git Workflow
+
+- **Default branch**: `develop`
+- **PRs target `develop`** (trunk-based development)
+- **Branch naming**: `users/<github-username>/<branch-name>`
+- **Sync**: `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/develop` (avoid merge)
+- **CODEOWNERS**: `.github/CODEOWNERS` at root; some projects have their own
+- **git blame**: Run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs` to hide formatting-only commits
+
+## Sparse Checkout
+
+For working on specific projects without cloning everything:
+
+```bash
+git clone --no-checkout --filter=blob:none https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-systems.git
+cd rocm-systems
+git sparse-checkout init --cone
+git sparse-checkout set projects/rocprofiler-sdk shared/ctest
+git checkout develop
+```
+
+## CI
+
+- **GitHub Actions**: `.github/workflows/` — per-project workflows (build, formatting, Python linting, code coverage, CodeQL)
+- **Azure Pipelines**: External CI dispatched via `Dispatch Azure CI` action; builds on Ubuntu 22.04 for gfx942/gfx90a
+- **TheRock CI**: Build system integration tests in `test/therock/`
+- PR auto-labeling via `.github/labeler.yml` and CODEOWNERS
+
+## Project-Specific Notes
+
+Several projects have their own `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md` files with project-specific guidance:
+- `projects/amdsmi/CLAUDE.md` — API cascade rules, auto-generated wrapper warnings
+- `projects/hipfile/CLAUDE.md` — build and Python bindings instructions
+- `projects/rocprofiler-compute/AGENTS.md` — Python style, Ruff, PR workflow rules
